  "story": {
    "day": 100,
    "title": "Kaya's Museum Day",
    "sentences": [
      "Kaya, a junior high school student, woke up late on June twenty-second, two thousand twenty-two.",
      "Her dad was ready for their trip to the central international museum.",
      "\"We can't be late for the special meeting,\" he said.",
      "Kaya would love to see the Mt. Fuji exhibit on the fifth floor.",
      "It had many bird paintings, maybe from the fifteenth century.",
      "On the second floor, a big sale began on the fourth or tenth.",
      "Kaya helped Dad pick twelve clean plates and a towel.",
      "He roasted forty chicken pieces. Kaya made iced tea for the river picnic.",
      "\"Wow, whose beautiful artwork is theirs?\" she asked, trying not to touch.",
      "Everybody enjoyed it, but a noisy interviewer made Kaya sing a song.",
      "She remembered a headache from babysitting last February, hoping nothing else would change.",
      "\"Ours is better,\" Dad sang a song, \"than beach skiing or skating.\""
    ]
  }
}